<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's NLCF to seek 40,000T of soymeal, others.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's NLCF to seek 40,000T of soymeal, others.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's National Livestock Cooperatives Federation (NLCF) would invite tenders to buy 40,000 tonnes of soybean meal by 11:00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, an NLCF official said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The NLCF official said it would also invite tenders to buy 10,000 tonnes or 15,000 tonnes of palm kernel meal, and 20,000 tonnes of wheat bran pellet.</p>
<p>The NLCF will re-invite the tenders on August 26 and 29, if it passes on the tenders on Tuesday due to high prices.</p>
<p>Details for the tenders are:</p>
<p>-- Soymeal  POSITION		   TONNE  SHIPPING	     ARRIVAL/PORTS</p>
<p>India or S.America One  40,000 Oct 4-23/Sep 7-26  Nov 10/Inchon,Kunsan,Ulsan</p>
<p>-- Palm kernel meal</p>
<p> One			 10,000  Sep 8-27	     Oct</p>
<p>10/Inchon,Kunsan,Ulsan</p>
<p>or</p>
<p> Two			 5,000   Aug 29-Sep 17	Sep</p>
<p>30/Inchon</p>
<p> Three		     5,000   Sep 28-Oct 17	Oct 30/Ulsan</p>
<p> Four			5,000   Sep 28-Oct 17	Oct</p>
<p>30/Kunsan</p>
<p>-- Wheat bran pellet</p>
<p> One			10,000   Oct 19-Nov 7	 Nov</p>
<p>20/Inchon</p>
<p> Two			10,000   Sep 18-Oct 7	 Oct</p>
<p>20/Ulsan/Kunsan</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
